# 8. Stage 6 — Azure Functions Ingestion Pipeline

Deploy three Azure Functions as the ingestion pipeline. The pipeline logic (file detection, validation, staging, promotion) is unchanged from the existing pipeline scripts. Only the execution host and trigger mechanism change.

## 8.1 Function Definitions

| **Function Name** | **Trigger Type** | **Behaviour** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| obs_actuals_ingestion | Timer trigger — cron: 0 0 * * * * (every hour on the hour) | Scans the landing-actuals Blob Storage container for new files not recorded in obs.ingestion_control. Processes all new files per pipeline step sequence. |
| obs_employees_ingestion | Timer trigger — cron: 0 0 2 * * * (daily at 02:00 UTC) | Scans the landing-employees container for new files and processes them. |
| obs_hierarchy_ingestion | Blob Storage trigger — fires on new blob created in landing-hierarchies container | Processes the triggering file immediately on arrival. |

| **Claude Code note — Azure Functions feasibility for this workload** | ***Azure Functions on a Consumption plan is well-suited to the OBS ingestion workload. Actuals files are processed hourly; employee files daily; hierarchy files ad hoc. None of these are high-frequency or long-running jobs. The Consumption plan******'******s 10-minute maximum execution timeout is sufficient for typical file volumes. If a single ingestion run exceeds 10 minutes due to an unusually large file, upgrade to a Premium plan (60-minute timeout) or Dedicated plan (unlimited). Monitor execution duration via Application Insights from day one.*** |
| --- | --- |

## 8.2 Repository Structure Changes for Azure Functions

Create a new top-level directory in the monorepo for the Azure Functions app. The existing pipeline scripts in backend/pipeline/ are refactored into Azure Functions entry points:

| **obs/ ├── pipeline-functions/          # NEW — Azure Functions app │   ├── host.json                # Functions host configuration │   ├── requirements.txt         # Pipeline-specific dependencies (psycopg2-binary, pandas, openpyxl, azure-storage-blob) │   ├── obs_actuals_ingestion/ │   │   ├── __init__.py          # Function entry point — calls actuals_pipeline.run() │   │   └── function.json        # Timer trigger binding definition │   ├── obs_employees_ingestion/ │   │   ├── __init__.py          # Function entry point — calls employees_pipeline.run() │   │   └── function.json        # Timer trigger binding definition │   └── obs_hierarchy_ingestion/ │       ├── __init__.py          # Function entry point — calls hierarchy_pipeline.run() │       └── function.json        # Blob Storage trigger binding definition └── backend/     └── pipeline/                # Existing — pipeline logic moved here unchanged         ├── actuals_pipeline.py  # Core logic; now called by the Function entry point         ├── employees_pipeline.py         └── hierarchy_pipeline.py** |
| --- |

