## 8.6 Idempotency Verification

Before activating production triggers, verify idempotency for each pipeline function:

- Drop a test actuals file into the landing-actuals container.

- Trigger obs_actuals_ingestion manually via the Azure Portal or Azure Functions Core Tools.

- Verify obs.ingestion_control has a COMPLETED record with the correct file_name and content_hash.

- Drop the same file again (identical content).

- Trigger obs_actuals_ingestion again. Verify: no duplicate records in obs.actuals; obs.ingestion_control shows the second run was skipped (file_name + content_hash already COMPLETED).

- Repeat this procedure for obs_employees_ingestion and obs_hierarchy_ingestion.

| **Claude Code note — PostgreSQL upsert idempotency** | ***The _pg_upsert() function uses INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE, which is inherently idempotent when the conflict target matches the natural deduplication key. The obs.ingestion_control file-level deduplication check (file_name + content_hash) is the first gate. If a file passes the gate, _pg_upsert() ensures that even if the pipeline runs the promotion step twice, no duplicate records are created. Both gates must be verified as described above.*** |
| --- | --- |

Stage 6 acceptance criteria:

- All three functions appear in the Azure Portal under obs-prod-pipeline with status Enabled.

- obs_actuals_ingestion runs on the hourly schedule — confirmed via execution history in Application Insights.

- obs_employees_ingestion runs on the daily schedule — confirmed via execution history.

- obs_hierarchy_ingestion fires within 60 seconds of a new blob appearing in landing-hierarchies.

- Idempotency verified for all three functions per Section 8.6 procedure.

- Pipeline errors (validation failures, file-level rejections) are delivered to the ALERT_CHANNEL (teams or email), not to console only.

# 9. Stage 7 — End-to-End Validation

Execute the following validation sequence in the production environment. This sequence follows the full budget cycle path and must be completed before any real users are provisioned.

| **Step** | **Action** | **Expected Result** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Authenticate as the first Administrator user | Entra ID login completes. OBS application shell loads. User's is_administrator flag is confirmed active via GET /api/v1/me. |
| 2 | Provision a second test user via the User Management screen | User record appears in obs.users in PostgreSQL. Audit log records the creation event. |
| 3 | Drop a cost center hierarchy CSV into the landing-hierarchies container | obs_hierarchy_ingestion fires within 60 seconds. obs.cost_center_hierarchy_nodes is populated. obs.ingestion_control records a COMPLETED entry. |
| 4 | Drop an account hierarchy CSV into the landing-hierarchies container | obs.expense_accounts and obs.account_hierarchy_nodes are populated. |
| 5 | Drop an employee file into landing-employees; trigger obs_employees_ingestion manually | obs.employees is populated. Dropping the same file again and re-triggering produces no duplicates. |
| 6 | Drop an actuals file into landing-actuals; trigger obs_actuals_ingestion manually | obs.actuals is populated. Quarantine cases appear in obs.quarantine. obs.ingestion_control records the run. |
| 7 | Enter a budget version and budget lines via the Budget Planning module | Budget lines are persisted in obs.budget_lines in PostgreSQL. Audit log records all mutations. |
| 8 | Submit the budget version via the Finance Approval Workflow | obs.finance_review_records is created. Finance Reviewer receives a notification in the in-application notification inbox. |
| 9 | Approve the budget as a Finance Reviewer | Budget version status updates to Approved. Audit log records the approval event. |
| 10 | Run an actuals vs budget report | Report renders with data from obs.actuals and obs.budget_lines. Excel export downloads a correctly formatted xlsx file within 10 seconds. |

