# 11. Migration Acceptance Criteria

All criteria below must pass before the migration is considered complete and production traffic is accepted.

| **AC-PG-ID** | **Acceptance Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-PG-01** | All obs.* tables exist in the PostgreSQL obs schema. SELECT COUNT(*) on every table returns without error. |
| **AC-PG-02** | The obs.audit_log immutable trigger is active. An UPDATE or DELETE against obs.audit_log returns an error from the trigger. |
| **AC-PG-03** | LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS is absent from all production and staging environment configurations. The startup assertion raises an error if LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true on a non-localhost host. |
| **AC-PG-04** | GET /health on the App Service API endpoint returns HTTP 200 with DB_ENGINE=postgresql active. |
| **AC-PG-05** | The Entra ID OIDC login flow completes for a provisioned OBS user. An Entra ID account with no obs.users record is denied with HTTP 403, not an application error. |
| **AC-PG-06** | CORS blocks requests from any origin other than the registered production frontend hostname. |
| **AC-PG-07** | No hardcoded credentials exist in any source file, configuration file, or CI/CD definition. |
| **AC-PG-08** | App Service resolves all Key Vault references successfully at startup — confirmed by the absence of Key Vault resolution errors in Application Insights. |
| **AC-PG-09** | The _pg_upsert() function produces no duplicate records when the merge() helper is called twice with the same records and key columns. |
| **AC-PG-10** | All three Azure Functions are deployed, enabled, and executing on their configured triggers. Idempotency verified per Section 8.6 for all three functions. |
| **AC-PG-11** | The full budget cycle end-to-end validation in Section 9 completes without error across all 10 steps. |
| **AC-PG-12** | Excel export produces a correctly formatted xlsx file within 10 seconds for a representative report dataset. |
| **AC-PG-13** | Application Insights receives telemetry (request traces, PostgreSQL dependency traces) within 5 minutes of the first authenticated API request. |
| **AC-PG-14** | make test-unit passes with zero failures after all code changes in Stage 4 are applied. |
| **AC-PG-15** | At least one active Administrator, one active fiscal year, one cost center hierarchy node, and one account hierarchy node exist in the production PostgreSQL database. |

