| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Confirm the target Azure region for all resources. | Infrastructure / project lead to confirm. |
| 2 | Confirm PostgreSQL SKU adequacy. Standard_D2s_v3 (2 vCores, 8 GB RAM) is specified. For 50–200 users with budget cycle load peaks, this is a reasonable starting point; validate under load testing and scale up if needed. | Development team to confirm via load testing in staging. |
| 3 | Confirm Azure Functions Consumption plan timeout is sufficient. If any single ingestion run is expected to exceed 10 minutes, upgrade to Premium plan before go-live. | Development team to measure pipeline execution time against representative file sizes. |
| 4 | Confirm PostgreSQL firewall strategy for Azure Functions. Dynamic outbound IPs on the Consumption plan may require VNet Integration for a stable firewall rule. Evaluate before Stage 2. | Infrastructure team to decide: VNet Integration vs Allow Azure Services. |
| 5 | schema/bootstrap_pg.sql must be authored (Stage 3) before Stages 4 through 7 can proceed. Assign this task explicitly. | Development team to author and peer-review before Stage 3 execution. |
| 6 | Confirm Microsoft Teams webhook URL or email SMTP configuration for the ALERT_CHANNEL pipeline notification target. | System administrator / IT to provide. |
| 7 | Confirm that all SQL in the existing pipeline scripts uses named placeholders compatible with psycopg2 %(name)s syntax, or schedule the SQL placeholder audit described in Section 6.6. | Development team to complete audit before Stage 5 deployment. |

